<title>GERMANY: Toepfer sees higher Chinese soybeans, meal imports.</title>
<headline>Toepfer sees higher Chinese soybeans, meal imports.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>China may import between one and 1.5 million tonnes of soybeans and more than two million tonnes of soymeal in the 1996/97 season, grain trader Toepfer said in a monthly report.</p>
<p>In 95/96, China became a net importer of beans and meal for the first time, Toepfer said.</p>
<p>Imports of 700,000 tonnes of soybeans and 1.6 million tonnes of soymeal compared with 350,000 tonnes of bean exports and 150,000 tonnes of meal.</p>
<p>Toepfer said domestic meat demand was rising and this raised meals and feeds requirements.</p>
<p>Combined domestic rapeseed and soybean production this year had fallen short of last year's by 1.5 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
